--- Immutable manuscript lines 565-588 ---
565: It remains to check the network dimensions and link locality.  At a
566: gate, the common label $(\xi,\zeta)$ ranges over a polynomial set.
567: Choose one participating party and share this label along a star to
568: the other participating parties, using one virtual index of that
569: polynomial dimension on each star edge.  Each slot's sample index
570: $j\in\{1,\ldots,k\}$ is shared directly between its two endpoint
571: parties.  The local source matrices in
572: \eqref{eq:compression-random-source} are determined by these labels
573: and the fixed samples.  Put the gate's scalar coefficient and averaging
574: factors into any one local tensor.  All local maps, private source
575: preparations, intermediate memories, and final garbage traces can then
576: be contracted within each party to give a single tensor with its
577: physical ket and bra legs.  In particular, coordinates in the common
578: private direct sums are contracted locally and are not virtual link
579: indices.
580:
581: There are at most $b-1$ star links and $\binom b2$ sample links per
582: gate.  Every party belongs to at most $b$ nonprivate gates, so the
583: resulting network has bounded incidence.  Each link joins two
584: participants of one original gate.  Parallel links can be left
585: separate or combined; only boundedly many meet a party, so combining
586: them preserves a polynomial dimension bound.  Sampled tensor entries
587: need not be bounded.  Their existence and link dimensions, rather than
588: their numerical size or efficient computation, are what is required.
